@V := "tape" :: spec [active]
  version = "1.0"

@H 1173 := "MEMBRANE / self<->non-self boundary — does a maintained boundary (reject/flag non-self inputs) improve OOD robustness vs no boundary? (life-criterion MISSING #3: boundary)" :: universe [🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE — BOTH gates fail; membrane neither lowers in-dist error nor beats the dense raw-distance OOD discriminator]
  seed         = "Audit gap: a cell has a membrane defining inside (self) vs outside (non-self); the anima Psi=1/2 basin is an IMPLICIT boundary, not a maintained one. H_1143/1151 found the substrate has NO learned in/out familiarity handle — a membrane would supply it."
  substrate    = "toy $0 CPU 12 seeds, DIM=8, K_true=5. REUSE h1159b cells; ADD a maintained inclusion radius per cell (EMA of inlier dist, seed 2.0, 3x mult, gates only after an 800-step grace window so cells form first); inputs outside ALL radii = NON-SELF -> rejected (not adapted into the self manifold)."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-reg, VERBATIM): 🟢 BOUNDARY-HELPS iff (a) lowers in-distribution error vs no-boundary (Cohen's d>=0.8) AND (b) flags non-self/OOD at AUROC>=0.70 (the self/non-self discriminator the dense substrate lacked, cf H_1143). 🔴 if no robustness gain nor OOD-flag above bar (a_paper_negative_ok). Construction-defect fix BEFORE scoring: v1 enforced membrane from step 0 (radii tiny, cells unformed) -> boundary arm rejected everything, never converged (err 11.8); fixed with an 800-step learning grace + generous radius seed + a fair NEAR-OOD probe (shift 5) since the original FAR shift (14) made raw distance a trivially-perfect (control AUROC=1.0) discriminator."
  result       = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE — BOTH gates FAIL. (a) ROBUSTNESS FAIL: membrane RAISES in-dist err, never lowers it — clean d=-5.76 (err 1.64 noboundary vs 7.82 boundary), contam-15%-OOD d=-1.67 (err 1.64 vs 4.06); even where the membrane's whole job is rejecting non-self, the dense no-boundary substrate (1.64) still beats it (4.06). (b) OOD-FLAG FAIL: on the fair NEAR-OOD regime membrane AUROC=0.540 (~chance) while the dense raw-distance CONTROL=0.9998 — the membrane is FAR WORSE than the discriminator the dense substrate already has geometrically; even on trivial FAR-OOD membrane=0.847 < control=1.000."
  finding      = "A maintained membrane adds NOTHING over the dense substrate and actively DEGRADES both fit and OOD-detection. KEY tie to H_1143: H_1143 found no LEARNED input-familiarity handle, but a simple GEOMETRIC raw nearest-cell distance already separates non-self near-perfectly (AUROC ~1.0) at this toy scale — there is no in/out signal MISSING for a membrane to supply, and gating on a maintained radius only throws away legitimate self-adaptation. Boundary as an EXPLICIT maintained structure is ruled out as a robustness lever at toy scale; the implicit Psi=1/2 basin + raw distance already suffice."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (toy $0 12-seed; a_paper_negative_ok). gate_a FAIL (d<0.8, sign negative) · gate_b FAIL (near-AUROC 0.540 < 0.70 and << dense control 0.9998)."
  scope        = "toy; live engine + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). p7, AUROC not perplexity."
  artifacts    = "UNIVERSE/h1173_membrane_self_nonself.py · .verdicts/1173_membrane_self_nonself/H_1173.txt"
  xref         = "h1143-hidden-ood-metacog · h1151-dg-pattern-separation · h1159b_mitosis_capacity_self_tuning · a_core_engine_map · a_paper_negative_ok · p7"
